SCOPE TEXT: recursively collect all strings from the record (depth-limited), but classify markers only on a curated set of fields:
  scope, summary, statement, description, authority_note, independence_note, non_claims, not_claimed, findings, checks, notes, review_note, method, coverage, verdict_note
LIMITATION MARKERS (case-insensitive):
  M1 r"\bSCOPED\b"
  M2 r"covers\s+ONLY"
  M3 r"not\s+the\s+full\s+schema"
  M4 r"remains\s+the\s+binding\s+coverage"
  M5 r"blind\s+full-schema"
  M6 r"\b(repair|visibility|strictness|axis|delta|mechanical|cross-artifact|component)[- ]scope\b"
  M7 r"scope\s*[:=].{0,40}\b(only|not|no semantic|mechanical|structural)\b"
  M8 r"\bthis verdict covers\b"
  M9 r"not\s+a\s+(semantic|full-schema|G-FORM)\b"
  M10 r"\bexcludes\b"
FULL-SCHEMA MARKERS:
  F1 counts_as_full_schema_verdict == True
  F2 r"full[- ]schema (verdict|review|accept)"
  F3 r"\bG-FORM verdict\b"
  F4 r"\ball\s+\d+\s+conformance checks pass\b"
  F5 r"blind\s+full-schema" (careful: that's a limitation marker in worker-061; only use as full marker if not negated)
