To keep this defensible and conservative, I'll use a two-tier rule:
  - **Hard scope limitation** (disqualifying): text matching (a) r"covers\s+ONLY\b", (b) r"not\s+the\s+full\s+schema", (c) r"remains\s+the\s+binding\s+coverage", (d) r"scope\s*[:=]\s*[^.;]{0,80}\bonly\b" (scope field explicitly ".. only"), (e) r"\bthis verdict covers\b[^.;]{0,80}\b(only|excluding)\b", (f) target_id naming a *derived/candidate* artifact rather than the schema (e.g., "repair candidate", "candidate", "sandbox", "delta", "#...rev" with a different hash). 
